course: dictionary
lesson: 1819
title: Cluster: a group close together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cluster is a group of similar things close together. Read the context: «Ladybirds hibernate together in clusters in sheltered spots like window frames.» The words together and sheltered show that a cluster is a tight group of ladybirds, not one lonely ladybird.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Stars born from the same cloud often stay together for a while as a cluster.» If cluster means a close group, the sentence still makes sense: the stars stay as a close group for a while.
explain: Cluster can also be a verb. People cluster round something when they gather close together. In maths, a cluster is where many dots on a graph group together, and in phonics a consonant cluster is a group of consonants like «str» in «string».
fact: A cluster is a group of similar things close together.
fact: «Ladybirds» hibernate together in clusters in sheltered spots, which helps them stay warm and safe.
fact: «Stars» born from the same cloud can stay together as a cluster, like the Pleiades.
fact: To cluster means to gather or stay close together in a group.
fact: A consonant cluster is a group of consonant letters together in a word, like «str» in «string».
exercise: «Ladybirds hibernate together in clusters in sheltered spots.» What is a cluster here? | A flying insect | A type of window frame | *A group of similar things close together | A single ladybird on its own
exercise: Which of these is a consonant cluster? | th in think | *str in string | ai in rain | ee in tree
exercise: Tom says people cluster round the teacher. What does cluster mean here? | Fall fast asleep | Walk away quickly | *Gather close together in a group | Count each one carefully
test: Which word in «Stars born from the same cloud often stay together for a while as a cluster» means a close group? | cloud | together | *cluster | Stars
test: On a graph, many dots grouped tightly together form what? | A single dot | Empty space | *A cluster | A blank title
exam: The Pleiades is a cluster of stars about 100 million years old. What does cluster mean in this sentence? | A line drawn across a page | A loud noise | *A close group of similar things | Only one star
